          "title": "compatibilism",
          "url": "https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/compatibilism/",
          "score": 0.54133517,
          "snippet": "Compatibilism asserts that free will and moral responsibility are compatible with determinism by redefining control through mechanisms such as reasons-responsiveness, hierarchical models of desire, and Strawsonian reactive attitudes. This position challenges incompatibilist arguments regarding alternative possibilities and the Consequence Argument by focusing on an agent's internal dispositions and guidance control rather than the ability to do otherwise. The framework has evolved from classical empiricist accounts to modern revisions incorporating dispositionalist theories."
        },
        {
