          "snippet": "Kant argues that while Hume correctly identifies the lack of empirical basis for causal necessity, he erroneously reduces it to subjective custom; Kant contends instead that causality and necessary connection are a priori categories contributed by the mind. This transcendental framework allows pure concepts to convert subjective perceptions into objective experience with strict universality, thereby grounding scientific knowledge in principles rather than mere induction."
        },
        {
          "corpus_id": "raptor-subset-off",
