          "score": 0.676651,
          "snippet": "Heidegger reorients hermeneutics from Husserl's epistemological foundations to fundamental ontological inquiries into human existence, arguing that the phenomenological epoché is inadequate for capturing factual lived experience. He posits that self-interpretation is inherently difficult due to worldly involvement, social averaging, and historical tradition, a view later expanded by Paul Ricoeur through his analysis of language and narrative."
        },
        {
          "corpus_id": "raptor-subset-off",
          "title": "husserl",
